    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0110" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg30"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 46.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The President having been advised that the
                    Government of Austria-Hungary is about to be represented in the United States by
                    an ambassador extraordinary and plenipotentiary, he has, under authority
                    conferred upon him by the Congress of the United States <pb facs="0111" n="31"
                        xml:id="pg31"/> and in recognition of the friendly intention of the
                    Austro-Hungarian Government, appointed you, by and with the advice and consent
                    of the Senate, to be ambassador extraordinary and plenipotentiary of the United
                    States to Austria-Hungary.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
